<https://w3id.org/seas/SystemOntology>
        a       <http://purl.org/vocommons/voaf#Vocabulary> ;
        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator>
                <http://maxime-lefrancois.info#me> ;
        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description>
                "The System Ontology defines Systems, Connections between systems, and Connection Points at which systems may be connected. This ontology is then specialized for multiple domains. For example:\n\n- In electric energy: \n    - power systems consume, produce, store, and exchange electricity;\n    - power connections are where electricity flows between systems;\n    - power connection points are plugs, sockets, or power busses.\n- In the electricity market:\n    - players and markets are systems;\n    - connections are contracts or transactions between two players, or between a player and a market;\n    - connection points include offers and bids."@en ;
        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued>
                "2016-06-06"^^xsd:date ;
        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language>
                <http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng> ;
        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified>
