                  <http://purl.org/stuff/rev#text>
                          "Seems obsolete and replaced by http://www.w3.org/2002/12/cal/icaltzd, used in the W3C note (2005-09-29) at http://www.w3.org/TR/rdfcal/. But neither vocabulary makes any reference to the other one. http://www.w3.org/2002/12/cal/icaltzd has been removed from LOV because the file contains errors, but this namespace seems nevertheless still used by applications such as Tabulator (source : Masahide Kansaki)"
